    {
      "sentence_id": 26,
      "text": "CHETLURU SREENIVAS presented this Petition under Article 226 of the Constitution of India praying that in the circumstances stated in the affidavit filed therewith, the High Court may be pleased to issue an order, direction or Writ, more particularly one in the nature of Writ of Mandamus, declaring the action of the respondents in not depositing the enhanced compensation amounts to the petitioners for acquiring the lands, as laid down by the Honble Supreme Court of India in the cases reported in AIR 1988 SC 2123 (K.Krishna Reddy and others Vs.Special Deputy Collector, Land Acquisition Unit II, Karimhagar) and in AIR 2012 SC 1624 (Premji Nathu v. State of Gujarat Anr.), as illegal, void,\narbitrary, unfair, unjust, against the provisions of a welfare legislation, namely. Land Acquisition Act 1894, and unconstitutional, being violative of rights of the petitioners enshrined under Art. 14,\n21 300A of the Constitution of India, and consequently direct the respondents to deposit compensation to the petitioners as ordered in Judgement dated 30-11-2023 passed in LAOP No. 79 of 2011 in accordance with law and pass such other order or orders may deem fit and proper in the circumstances of the case AND WHEREAS the High Court upon perusing the petition and affidavit of grounds filed herein and upon hearing the arguments of Sri CHETLURU SREENIVAS Advocate for the Petitioner, G.P for Revenue for Respondent Nos. 1 to 4 , GP for Irrigation for respondent No.5, GP for Finance for respondent No.6, GP for General Administration for respondent No.7,\ndirected issue of notice to the Respondents herein to show cause as to why this WRIT PETITION should not be admitted.",
